<p>This notice explains how <strong>cizgifikrim.net</strong> processes personal information. The data controller is <strong>Aras Tokdemir (CizgiFikrim, Istanbul)</strong>. Contact: <a href="mailto:cizgifikrimnet@gmail.com">cizgifikrimnet@gmail.com</a>.</p>
<div class="legal-kutu">We do not use advertising trackers or cookies. Information submitted through our form is used to respond to your enquiry. Enquiry records are deleted after 12 months. First-party visit measurement respects Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.</div>
<h2>1. Information we process</h2><ul><li><strong>Contact form:</strong> name, email, message, selected topic, source page, any campaign parameters, consent time and notice version. Abuse prevention uses an irreversible hash of the IP address, not the address itself in the enquiry record. No phone number is requested.</li><li><strong>Meeting calendar:</strong> information you submit to Cal.com, including name, email, meeting type, time and other booking details.</li><li><strong>Email:</strong> your email address and correspondence.</li><li><strong>Visit measurement:</strong> anonymous site-use records described below.</li><li><strong>Infrastructure logs:</strong> hosting providers may keep standard access logs containing IP address, browser information and timestamps.</li></ul>
<h2>2. Purposes</h2><p>We use information to reply to enquiries and arrange meetings, protect forms against spam and abuse, and understand which pages are useful. The form checkbox records consent for the stated processing. You may withdraw consent at any time. We do not sell your information, add you to marketing lists or use it for advertising.</p>
<h2>3. Service providers and location</h2><ul><li><strong>Supabase:</strong> enquiry, booking and measurement records, hosted in Frankfurt in the European Union.</li><li><strong>Cal.com:</strong> meeting bookings are also subject to Cal.com’s own privacy policy. A booking summary is stored in our database.</li><li><strong>GitHub Pages:</strong> website hosting.</li></ul><p>Some providers are outside Türkiye. The form consent includes processing and storage with the providers described here.</p>
<h2>4. Retention</h2><p>Enquiry records, their IP hashes, booking records and email correspondence are retained for 12 months. Visit measurement records are retained for no more than 180 days. You may request earlier deletion by email. Where a business relationship is established, statutory retention periods for contracts and accounting records apply separately.</p>
<h2>5. Cookies, measurement and preferences</h2><p>We do not use cookies. Our first-party measurement records page paths without query strings, external referral information, mobile/desktop viewport, time on page and clicked link or button labels. Records are not linked to your name or email and are not shared with advertising networks. A random session identifier, <code>cf_sid</code>, is kept in <code>sessionStorage</code> and disappears when the tab closes. Measurement is disabled when Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control is enabled.</p><p>Your selected language is stored locally as <code>cf_language</code>, with the value <code>tr</code> or <code>en</code>. It is a preference, not a visitor identifier. You may remove it by clearing browser storage. Theme preference is read from your device and is not stored by this site.</p>
<h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Under Article 11 of Türkiye’s Personal Data Protection Law (KVKK), you may request information about whether and how your data is processed; its purposes and recipients; correction or deletion where applicable; notification of those changes to recipients; object to an adverse outcome resulting from automated analysis; and seek compensation for unlawful processing. Email your request to us. We respond within 30 days. You may complain to the Turkish Personal Data Protection Board if you are not satisfied with our response.</p>
<h2>7. Changes</h2><p>We update the date above when this notice changes. Product-specific privacy notices on linked services apply to those products.</p>
<h2 id="iletisim-formu">8. Contact form consent</h2><p>By checking the form’s consent box, you confirm that you have read this notice and consent to processing for the purposes described. The time of consent and the notice version are saved with the enquiry.</p><p><strong>Version: gizlilik-2026-11</strong> · <code>consent_version</code>: gizlilik-2026-11</p><p><a href="{{ links.terms }}">Terms of use</a></p>
